WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.460
Welcome to SimplyFile, the income-tax filing portal for CA firms. This is Demo C A Filing Firm, approved by the portal admin. Every client and figure you will see is made up for this demo.

2
00:00:16.063 --> 00:00:26.673
My firm shows the firm's approval, its papers and its team. The shield is green: the firm is approved, so the Filing screens are open.

3
00:00:27.297 --> 00:00:32.867
Kavitha joins as a partner: she can sign off, file and revise.

4
00:00:37.563 --> 00:00:42.983
Anand is the reviewer: he reads everything and signs off the computation.

5
00:00:47.641 --> 00:00:55.491
Ravi is the tax preparer: clients, mapping, reconciling and computing - no sign-off or filing.

6
00:00:57.655 --> 00:01:06.845
Each person gets a one-time password and sets their own at first sign-in. Their role decides which menus and buttons they see.

7
00:01:07.452 --> 00:01:16.742
Client one is a Hindu undivided family with a trading business and a tax audit: the full road from the client master to a filed return.

8
00:01:17.344 --> 00:01:33.374
A new client: name, status, PAN - its fourth letter must fit the status - email, phone, address and the bank account for the refund. Date of birth, the karta's father's name and PAN go into the return's verification.

9
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:59.719
Into assessment year 2026-27 with ITR-3 and a tax audit, assigned to Ravi. The stage is not picked by anyone - it moves by itself.

10
00:02:00.327 --> 00:02:08.367
Intake: upload the client's statement - the income statement, depreciation and loans - straight from Excel.

11
00:02:08.969 --> 00:02:19.869
Every row is grouped under the statement's own headings. Each heading adds up the way the statement means it, and is checked against the statement's own total.

12
00:02:20.469 --> 00:02:29.109
SimplyFile has already suggested an SF Ref for almost every row. Accept them all in one click.

13
00:02:29.719 --> 00:02:40.859
One row needs a person: the disallowance under section forty a, i a. It goes to business income - type ITR3 BP and save.

14
00:02:41.469 --> 00:02:51.599
The client's final accounts next: trading, profit and loss, and the balance sheet. Their own SF Ref column tags every row.

15
00:02:52.202 --> 00:03:03.382
Uploading the same statement again does not fail: SimplyFile offers to replace it, keeps the refs on rows that did not change, and keeps the old version.

16
00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:12.123
Reconcile: bring in the 26AS, AIS and TIS downloaded from the income-tax portal.

17
00:03:17.219 --> 00:03:28.719
Books against the portal, deductor by deductor. One red: Lakshmi Finance shows thirty-six thousand of TDS, the books claim forty thousand.

18
00:03:29.313 --> 00:03:37.403
Explain it - the client confirmed the credit as per 26AS - and the year moves on to review by itself.

19
00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:47.380
Compute: each head adds its mapped rows. Tax, surcharge and cess, under the regime you pick.

20
00:03:47.983 --> 00:04:03.993
Interest under 234 A, B and C is worked out from the 26AS challans by date - here nil, the advance tax covered every instalment. The refund is sixty-six thousand three hundred and sixty rupees.

21
00:04:04.608 --> 00:04:24.988
The files for filing: the computation in Excel, the ITR-3 JSON in the income-tax department's own format, and the Form 3CB-3CD JSON - each checked against the CBDT schema before you download. The balance sheet tallies and the profit matches business income.

22
00:04:25.594 --> 00:04:37.814
The reviewer signs off, then the acknowledgement number and the date filed. Filed on time, it is an original return under 139 one, and the year locks.

23
00:04:38.422 --> 00:04:52.682
Found a mistake after filing? Start a revised return. Changed your mind? Discard the revision - the filed return stands. Nothing filed is ever deleted.

24
00:04:53.297 --> 00:05:02.637
Client two, Ramesh Iyer, was born in 1958: a resident senior citizen with no business income, filing late.

25
00:05:31.655 --> 00:05:38.495
His income statement and 26AS - every row suggested, accepted in one click.

26
00:05:47.797 --> 00:06:05.217
A senior citizen with no business income pays no advance tax, so no interest under 234 B or C. Filing after the 31st of July due date still costs 234 A: five hundred and seventy-one rupees, worked out to the day.

27
00:06:05.828 --> 00:06:17.658
Client three is a partnership firm: ITR-5 with a tax audit and Form 3CEB for transfer pricing. Its partners go in the client master.

28
00:07:00.547 --> 00:07:14.057
Its statement and its final accounts. These accounts have no SF Ref column at all - SimplyFile reads the words under the P and L and balance sheet headings and suggests every ref.

29
00:07:25.594 --> 00:07:29.654
26AS in, everything agrees.

30
00:07:31.094 --> 00:07:47.914
Advance tax fell short, so 234 B and 234 C apply: twenty-two thousand three hundred and seventy-two, and fourteen thousand one hundred and thirteen. With Form 3CEB the due date is the 30th of November.

31
00:07:48.516 --> 00:07:58.596
The ITR-5 JSON and the 3CB-3CD JSON, both checked against the department's schema - our firm named as the auditor.

32
00:07:59.219 --> 00:08:07.839
Client four, Kiran Kumar Rao, is a professional whose clients deducted TDS under 194 J.

33
00:08:47.797 --> 00:08:56.657
The 87 A rebate brings his tax to nil, so all the TDS comes back: a refund of one lakh eighty thousand.

34
00:08:57.266 --> 00:09:04.486
Filed on the 20th of August, within the new 31st of August due date for business returns.

35
00:09:06.266 --> 00:09:16.896
The refund was paid on the 1st of October. Interest under 244 A at half a percent a month: six thousand three hundred rupees.

36
00:09:17.516 --> 00:09:30.306
Client five, Meera Nair, filed her return for assessment year 2025-26 in July 2025. Later she found income she had missed.

37
00:09:55.422 --> 00:10:00.442
First the return as she filed it, with its 26AS.

38
00:10:15.203 --> 00:10:22.063
Recorded as filed on the 28th of July 2025: an original return.

39
00:10:26.141 --> 00:10:36.871
The 31st of December has passed, so a revised return is no longer allowed - SimplyFile offers an updated return, ITR-U, instead.

40
00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:41.440
The missed income goes in like any other statement.

41
00:10:50.234 --> 00:11:06.724
The updated return: two lakh sixty thousand six hundred and ninety-three of further tax, and under section 140 B an additional twenty-five percent - sixty-five thousand one hundred and seventy-three. Confirm it, sign off, and file.

42
00:11:07.328 --> 00:11:14.648
Back in Clients and years, every client shows where it stands, and the pipeline counts them by stage.

43
00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:29.909
Lost on any screen? Guide me walks you through it, step by step. SimplyFile - from the client's Excel to the department's JSON, for your whole firm. Thank you for watching.
